Not upstream (no QTBUG, unfixed on qtbase dev as of 2026-11). Same kind of guard as qtbase
c8943447d353 "iOS: Guard against hover events during window destruction". Drop this patch
when moving to a Qt release whose -[QUIView handlePresses:eventType:] checks platformWindow.
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: Guard against key presses during window destruction

UIKit delivers pressesEnded to the responder that received pressesBegan. When
the key press closes a window (a QShortcut or a dialog's Escape/Enter on press),
~QIOSWindow clears the QUIView's platformWindow, and the release reaches
handlePresses, which only checked qApp->focusWindow() and then dereferenced the
null platformWindow: EXC_BAD_ACCESS at 0x18 in -[QUIView handlePresses:eventType:]
<- -[QUIView pressesEnded:withEvent:]. Returning false passes the presses on to
the next responder.

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/ios/quiview.mm b/src/plugins/platforms/ios/quiview.mm
index 2d22362..c357fc4 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/ios/quiview.mm
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/ios/quiview.mm
@@ -672,7 +672,7 @@ inline ulong getTimeStamp(UIEvent *event)
     // this event will cause the application to return to Headboard (tvOS launcher).
     // When handling the event (for example, as a back button), both press and
     // release events must be handled accordingly.
-    if (!qApp->focusWindow())
+    if (!self.platformWindow || !qApp->focusWindow())
         return false;
 
     bool eventHandled = false;
